  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&#x201c;Providing Positive Life Alternatives to Egyptian Youth&#x201d; (PLAY 2)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The &#x201c;Providing Positive Life Alternatives to Egyptian Youth&#x201d; (PLAY) project overall objective is to contribute to curbing irregular migration of Egyptian youth by providing positive alternatives in the tourism sector. It seeks to integrate GoE responses to the phenomenon of irregular migration from Egypt, using a comprehensive approach that looks at different axes: a) Enhancing the quality of the vocational education to meet international standards; b) Identifying and training young Egyptians on skills and knowledge required by the labour market in Egypt and elsewhere to enhance their employability, and decrease the skills mismatch between job seekers and employers, and c); inform young Egyptians on risks of irregular migration and alternative regular routes.</narrative>
  </description>
